<type>(<scope>): <summary>

Why:
  <the problem this solves, or the reason the change is needed>

What:
  - <one bullet per logical change>

Verify:
  - <exact command> -> <observed result>

Refs: <design doc section / issue / task id>

# =====================================================================
#  abx commit template -- see AGENTS.md ("提交纪律")
# =====================================================================
#
#  SUBJECT  <type>(<scope>): <summary>
#    - imperative mood, lowercase summary, no trailing period
#    - 72 characters maximum
#    - <scope> is optional, e.g. feat(core):, fix(mounts):
#
#  TYPES
#    feat      a new capability
#    fix       a bug fix
#    refactor  behaviour-preserving restructure
#    perf      performance improvement
#    test      tests only
#    docs      documentation only
#    build     build system or dependencies
#    ci        CI configuration
#    chore     maintenance that fits nothing above
#    style     formatting only
#    revert    revert a previous commit
#
#  RULES
#    1. English only. CJK characters are rejected.
#    2. "Why:" and "What:" sections are mandatory.
#    3. "Verify:" is expected -- record the command and its real result.
#    4. One logical change per commit. Do not batch unrelated changes.
#    5. Blank line between the subject and the body.
#
#  These comment lines are stripped by git and never enter the message.
# =====================================================================
